  <div class="section-title">Message from the VICE-CHANCELLOR</div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>SASTRA makes significant contributions, not just to the advancement of education, but also to a variety of ways to societal welfare, promotion of culture, sensitizing the state and civil society on variety of pressing issues and so on. Towards these objectives, several schemes were drawn.</p>
    <p>SASTRA Conferred Doctor of Letters (honoris causa) on the three eminent personalities hailing from the erstwhile composite Thanjavur district on the occasion of the Holy Mahamaham, on February 17, 2016. Shri N. Gopalaswamy, former Chief Election Commissioner, and Dr. K. Sudhakar, and Dr. K. Sudhakar were among them. Dr. K. Sudhakar was honored with the degree of Doctor of Letters (honoris causa) on the occasion of the Holy Mahamaham.</p>
    <p>We wish it a lifetime opportunity to serve the humanity during the holy Mahamaham festival held at Kumbakonam. Nearly one lakh devotees were served meals at our Kumbakonam Campus for four days during the Mahamaham. SASTRA also rendered technical assistance to the Police Department in crowd monitoring during the festival, with its image processing and video analytics technology. We are extremely proud of this achievement.</p>
    <p>SASTRA University is much beholden to its founder Chancellor Late Shri S. Ramachandra Iyer. Without his extraordinary commitment and initiatives, the institution would not have achieved its present glory. In order to celebrate the centenary year in a grand manner, SASTRA organized a series of events.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">SPECIAL CONVOCATION & LATE SHRI S. RAMACHANDRA IYER CENTENARY CELEBRATIONS</div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>A Special Convocation, on the occasion of the Holy Mahamaham, was held at the Srinivasa Ramanujan Centre of SASTRA University, Kumbakonam on February 17, 2016. Late Shri S. Ramachandra Iyer Centenary Celebrations (in memory of the Founder-Chancellor of SASTRA University) was also launched on the occasion.</p>
    <p>Dr. S. S. Badrinath, Chairman Emeritus, Sankara Netralaya, Chennai delivered the Convocation Address and conferred the Doctor of Letters (honoris causa) on three eminent personalities hailing from the erstwhile composite Thanjavur district: Shri N. Gopalaswamy, former Chief Election Commissioner, Dr. K. Sudhakar, and Dr. K. Sudhakar.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="two-column">
    <div class="column">
      <div class="section-title">Convocation Highlights</div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>Dr. S. S. Badrinath, Chairman Emeritus, Sankara Netralaya, Chennai delivered the Convocation Address and conferred the Doctor of Letters (honoris causa) on three eminent personalities hailing from the erstwhile composite Thanjavur district: Shri N. Gopalaswamy, former Chief Election Commissioner, Dr. K. Sudhakar, and Dr. K. Sudhakar.</p>
        <p>The Convocation Ceremony was graced by the presence of various dignitaries.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <div class="section-title">Centenary Celebrations</div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>The Centenary Celebrations were organized to commemorate the life and legacy of Late Shri S. Ramachandra Iyer. Various cultural and academic events were held.</p>
        <p>The celebrations included lectures, seminars, and cultural programs, attracting a large number of attendees.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer">
    SASTRA UNIVERSITY
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center;">
    <div class="header-title">ITIHAS VOL. 16, I QUARTER - 2016</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Convocation Ceremony</div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>Dr. Badrinath said that all the three recipients of the honorary doctorate degrees are natives of composite Thanjavur district and have achieved eminence from humble beginnings. He appealed to the youth who attended the convocation to emulate the three and take them as role models.</p>
    <p>Dr. S. Vaidhyasubramaniam, Dean-Planning and Development, SASTRA read out the citations.</p>
    <p>Prof. R. Sethuraman, Vice Chancellor welcomed the gathering and Dr. S. S. Swaminathan, Dean - Sponsored Research proposed a vote of thanks.</p>
    <p>Many prominent citizens of Kumbakonam attended the function.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="two-column">
    <div class="column">
      <div class="section-title">Convocation Details</div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>SASTRA University has conferred the Degree of Doctor of Letters (honoris causa) to Dr. Kudavaiyal M. Balasubramanian for the exemplary research and work on temple architecture that stands as a testimony to Indian Culture. The exceptional commitment to unravel the minutiae of temple sculpture, painting and music, the passionate and illustrious career and work that provided the platform to the understanding of our rich Indian history, culture, fine arts and literature, and as SASTRA's homage to an academic scholar.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <div class="section-title">Convocation Details</div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>Shri Udayalukur K. Kalyanamaran receives the Degree of Doctor of Letters (honoris causa) to Shri Udayalukur K. Kalyanamaran with a deep sense of appreciation for his relentless pursuit in promoting traditional Bhajana Sampradaya amongst the old and the young alike, the initiatives to establish Bhajan Sampradaya as a viable tool for devotion and national integration and as SASTRA's homage to the exemplary services to the cultural heritage of India.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer">
    SASTRA UNIVERSITY
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center;">
    <div class="header-title">ITIHAS VOL. 16, I QUARTER - 2016</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Late Shri S. Ramachandra Iyer Centenary Celebrations</div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>Late Shri S. Ramachandra Iyer Centenary Celebrations are being organized throughout the year. As part of the events SASTRA will offer free surgery to around 150 children requiring critical cardiac, neural, ENT and other surgeries.</p>
    <p>The centenary celebrations also include cultural, educational scholarship, competitions to nurture nationalism, spiritualism and humanism besides other charitable activities.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="two-column">
    <div class="column">
      <div class="section-title">Special Medical Camp for Children</div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>SASTRA University organized a special medical camp for the children below the age of 15 years in Thanjavur district on January 23 & 24, 2016 as part of the Centenary celebrations of Late Shri S. Ramachandra Iyer.</p>
        <p>The camp was formally inaugurated by Dr. J.S.N. Moorthy, Vice-Chancellor, Shri Ramachandra Medical University, Chennai and Prof. R. Sethuraman, Vice Chancellor, SASTRA University.</p>
        <p>While inaugurating the camp, Prof. R. Sethuraman, said that from the camp 100 children from economically weak background in Thanjavur district, requiring surgery will be identified and the entire cost of surgery will be sponsored by SASTRA.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <div class="section-title">Centenary Celebrations Highlights</div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>The accompanying parents appreciated SASTRA for its special efforts to help the poor children of Thanjavur. A team of 15 doctors from Sri Ramachandra Medical University, specializing in different areas viz. Cardiology, Neurology, Pediatric, General medicine & Ophthalmology, participated in the camp.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer">
    SASTRA UNIVERSITY
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center;">
    <div class="header-title">ITIHAS VOL. 16, I QUARTER - 2016</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Mega Annadhanam by SASTRA University to Devotees of Mahamaham</div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>SASTRA University provided Annadhanam to around 1 lakh devotees of the Holy Mahamaham 2016, from February 19 to 22, 2016. The devotees who visited SASTRA campus in Kumbakonam during the Mahamaham festival were served traditional 'kalyana saapadu' in plantain leaf, prepared by Arusuvai Catering Services.</p>
    <p>A team of over 300 cooks, 700 servers and 1000 volunteers were engaged in this mammoth exercise.</p>
    <p>"Mahamaham is a lifetime opportunity to serve humanity and to this spiritual event that sees the convergence of lakhs of devotees without any invitation, offering delicious food is one of the finest ways of showing Kumbakonam's hospitality," said Prof. R. Sethuraman, Vice-Chancellor.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="two-column">
    <div class="column">
      <div class="section-title">Inauguration of Exhibition</div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>Shri Pon. Radhakrishnan, Union Minister of State for Road Transport, Highways & Shipping inaugurating the exhibition organised by Ministry of Information & Broadcasting, Govt. of India, at Kumbakonam in view of Mahamaham, in the presence of Prof. R. Sethuraman, Vice Chancellor, SASTRA on February 12, 2016.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <div class="section-title">Inauguration of Exhibition</div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>Shri Pon. Radhakrishnan and Prof. R. Sethuraman flagged off the awareness rally on "Clean India" in Kumbakonam in which 562 students of SASTRA participated. The rally started from Banadurai School and marched up to the Mahamaham Tank.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer">
    SASTRA UNIVERSITY
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center;">
